        {
          "type": "section",
          "text": "Everyone else"
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "text": "Count the bodies around me",
          "help": "How many people nearby have a Silhouette body, and in how many different presets. Each one, with its preset, is written to the Papyrus log.",
          "action": {
            "type": "CallGlobalFunction",
            "script": "Silhouette:Player",
            "function": "Census",
            "params": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "text": "Refresh the people around me",
          "help": "Everyone nearby keeps their preset but gets its values from this build again -- for after you edited a preset or rebuilt your bodies. Body morphs other mods add are left alone. With Silhouette.dll each keeps their own nipple and genital variety; without it the preset's values alone are written.",
          "action": {
            "type": "CallGlobalFunction",
            "script": "Silhouette:Player",
            "function": "Refresh",
            "params": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "text": "Give the people around me new bodies",
          "help": "Everyone nearby (never your character) rolls a new body, as if met for the first time, and the rules by name and faction get their say: someone a rule covers draws again from its presets. With Silhouette.dll, body morphs other mods keep under their own keyword are kept, and anyone in an AAF scene gets theirs when the scene ends; without it those morphs are cleared too. Cannot be undone.",
          "action": {
            "type": "CallGlobalFunction",
            "script": "Silhouette:Player",
            "function": "Reroll",
            "params": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "text": "Reset everyone",
          "help": "A fresh start: forgets every body Silhouette gave -- the ones you picked too -- and decides them all again, as if everyone were met for the first time. Named characters get their own body, the rules by name and faction draw again, everyone else rolls a new body from the pool. People around you change at once; everyone else the next time you meet them (the save remembers the reset). Body morphs other mods keep under their own keyword are kept. Press it twice to confirm. Cannot be undone. Needs Silhouette.dll and Silhouette.esp.",
          "action": {
            "type": "CallFunction",
            "form": "Silhouette.esp|802",
            "function": "MenuResetEveryone",
            "params": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "text": "Regeneration window"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "LooksMenu only shapes people who hold no body morphs at all, so someone another mod already marked (an AAF morph left by a scene) never gets a body. For 24 in-game hours after Silhouette first loads, such people around you are given one, and the other mod's morphs are kept. Needs Silhouette.esp."
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "text": "How is the regeneration window doing?",
          "help": "Open or closed, the in-game hours left, and how many people it has given a body.",
          "action": {
            "type": "CallGlobalFunction",
            "script": "Silhouette:Player",
            "function": "RegenerationStatus",
            "params": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "text": "Open a new 24-hour regeneration window",
          "help": "Starts another 24 in-game hours of giving bodies to people other mods marked first. People it already handled are not handled twice.",
          "action": {
            "type": "CallGlobalFunction",
            "script": "Silhouette:Player",
            "function": "OpenRegenerationWindow",
            "params": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
